{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): morning. cuff's done. blood pressure's one thirty eight over eighty two, pulse seventy six.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): yeah that's normal isn't it. i don't know why they've dragged me in.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): my sister's the same, hates these places. she had a migraine all weekend and still went into work. doctor's free.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (DOCTOR): right, mr hale. three months on from the mild stroke. any problems?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): i'm only here for the check after the stroke. there aren't problems. the hand's nothing.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (DOCTOR): left hand weaker?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): um, the left one's a tiny bit clumsy. drops the teaspoon. i still do the crossword, so.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): worse, or just the same since the stroke?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): same. since then. not worse. honestly it's fine.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): walking?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): walking's fine. paper shop most mornings.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): any limp? any falls?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): no. no limp and no falls.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): speech. any slurring?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): mm, i suppose. sometimes, not really. the wife says i mumble when the football's on.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): headaches? fits? blackouts?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): no. none of that.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): medicines. aspirin seventy five milligrams, atorvastatin eighty milligrams, amlodipine five milligrams. still taking the lot?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): yeah. uh aspirin in the morning, amlodipine five at breakfast, that's the blood pressure one. the atorvastin, i nearly said morning, no, that one's at night.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): any side effects?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): no. nothing.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): and the cholesterol, before the statin. what did they tell you?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): at the hospital they said it was borderline. that was their word. no actual number.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): squeeze my fingers. both hands.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): there. see, perfectly fine.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): left grip's a touch down. face is symmetrical. no arm drift.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): that clumsiness is the motor pathway after the stroke. the signals to the fingers don't get through quite cleanly. it is not a new stroke.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): if you say so. lot of fuss over a teaspoon.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): smoking? alcohol?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): packed the smoking in after the stroke. odd whisky at the weekend, nothing mad.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): i'll book a cholesterol blood test, and you're back here in six months. keep the tablets exactly as they are, and keep those morning walks. if the hand suddenly gets worse, or the speech goes, you come straight back, don't wait.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (NURSE): i'll get the blood form printed. my sister swears by her evening walk, mind, but that's her knees, not yours."
 ],
